        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): localize native app and watch surfaces",
        "body": "Part of #104979.\n\nAndroid runtime wiring landed separately in #105049.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where iOS and watchOS users selecting a supported non-English locale would still see English across setup, gateway, settings, chat, voice, notifications, Live Activities, Watch inbox, approval, and direct-connection surfaces.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nRoutes app-owned presentation copy through native localization, preserves backend/user/technical values verbatim, and generates deterministic runtime catalogs from the checked-in 21-locale translation inventory. Semantic Watch status payloads keep shipped text fields for staggered iPhone/watchOS updates, while generator checks reject new runtime interpolation and catalog drift.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. The branch was reviewed in bounded semantic, Watch protocol, Watch UI, and generator slices, with every accepted finding addressed before publication.\n\n## User Impact\n\niOS and watchOS surfaces now resolve translated app copy at runtime across all supported locales. Locale changes also re-render persisted Watch status and approval state instead of retaining sender-language strings.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node --import tsx scripts/apple-app-i18n.ts check`\n  - 1,189 iOS keys\n  - 4 macOS keys\n  - 84 InfoPlist localization files\n  - 21 locales\n- `node --import tsx scripts/native-app-i18n.ts check`\n  - 4,184 native inventory entries\n  - 21 locale artifacts\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxb914m9xgt18fdk13jtcdjn`\n  - `CI=true corepack pnpm test:serial test/scripts/apple-app-i18n.test.ts test/scripts/native-app-i18n.test.ts`\n  - 2 files passed, 24 tests passed\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- Focused autoreview slices: semantic, Watch protocol/UI, and generator slices clean on the exact tree.\n- Exact-head GitHub CI: pending.\n\nThe Linux Testbox cannot compile `apps/shared/OpenClawKit` because its `SwiftMath` dependency imports Apple-only `CoreGraphics`; exact-head macOS CI covers the Swift package and Apple application builds.\n",
        "branch": "fix/apple-watch-runtime-localization",
